Supported Compose files:
- compose.local-stack.yml: local laptop testing
- compose.synology.yml: Synology production

Local laptop test:
1. cp .env.example .env
2. Edit LABDB_STACK_DB_PASSWORD in .env
3. docker compose -f compose.local-stack.yml up -d db
4. docker compose -f compose.local-stack.yml run --rm web python manage.py migrate --noinput
5. docker compose -f compose.local-stack.yml run --rm web python manage.py createsuperuser
6. docker compose -f compose.local-stack.yml up web

Local reset, only for disposable test data:
docker compose -f compose.local-stack.yml down -v

Synology first deploy:
1. Put the project in /volume1/docker/flare-eln/project
2. Create folders:
   mkdir -p /volume1/docker/flare-eln/postgres-data
   mkdir -p /volume1/docker/flare-eln/backups
   mkdir -p /volume1/docker/flare-eln/external-imports
3. cp .env.synology.example .env
4. Edit .env with real NAS IP, secret key, DB user, and DB password
5. docker compose -f compose.synology.yml build web
6. docker compose -f compose.synology.yml up -d db
7. docker compose -f compose.synology.yml run --rm web python manage.py migrate --noinput
8. docker compose -f compose.synology.yml run --rm web python manage.py createsuperuser
9. docker compose -f compose.synology.yml up -d web

Private lab defaults:
1. Copy private/seed_lab_defaults.py to:
   /volume1/docker/flare-eln/external-imports/seed_lab_defaults.py
2. Run:
   docker compose -f compose.synology.yml run --rm web python /external-imports/seed_lab_defaults.py

Synology update:
bash scripts/update_synology_web.sh

Manual Synology backup:
bash scripts/backup_synology_db.sh

